{
  "id": "TikTokTopAdsTranscripts01",
  "name": "Transcribe TikTok Top Ads from the Creative Center to Google Sheets with Apify",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "sticky-main",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1200,
        -300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 700,
        "height": 1040,
        "content": "# Transcribe TikTok Top Ads from the Creative Center to Google Sheets with Apify\n\nPull the top-performing TikTok ads for an industry and region from the Creative Center and get what they say: the first-3-seconds hook, full transcript, CTR, likes, length and language, one row per ad.\n\n### Who it's for\nTikTok media buyers, UGC creators and creative strategists who want the scripts behind the ads that are already winning.\n\n### How it works\n1. A Set node holds the country code, period, industry and the number of ads to fetch.\n2. An HTTP Request starts the TikTok Creative Center Top Ads scraper on Apify, then an If node and a polling request wait until the run finishes.\n3. The run's dataset ID is handed to the TikTok Ads Transcript Scraper on Apify, so no ad rows pass through n8n. Each ad's audio is transcribed and the hook extracted. Music-only ads come back as uncharged misses.\n4. A Code node shapes one row per ad, a Set node tidies the columns and a Google Sheets node appends them.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create an HTTP Header Auth credential (name `Authorization`, value `Bearer YOUR_APIFY_TOKEN`) and select it on the three HTTP Request nodes.\n2. Connect Google Sheets and pick the spreadsheet and sheet.\n3. Open the Config node, choose the country, period, industry and how many ads to process.\n4. Run the workflow.\n\n### Requirements\nAn Apify account and a Google account.\n\n### Customization tips\nChange the industry or period to build a library per vertical. Sort by CTR in the Code node. Add a Schedule Trigger to refresh the top ads every week.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-sec-1",
      "name": "Section 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -480,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## 1. Configure\nYour input URL and item count live in one Set node."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-sec-2",
      "name": "Section 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -40,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 520,
        "content": "## 2. Scrape and wait\nStart the Apify scraper run, then poll it every few seconds until it finishes."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-sec-3",
      "name": "Section 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        400,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## 3. Transcribe and shape rows\nHand the run's dataset ID to the transcript actor, then build one row per item."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-sec-4",
